## PHASE 2 — Vital Simulator as Interim Data Source (Dev Mode only)

- Build a **realistic** vitals generator (plausible HR/SpO2/etc. ranges with natural variation and occasional threshold-breaching spikes — not flat/random noise).
- Simulator output must be pushed through **the exact same ingestion path** a real BLE reading would use: same payload schema, same `/api/health` endpoint, same validation, same downstream processing.
- Clearly label it **"DEV/SIMULATED"** in the UI wherever its data appears, tied to a `source: "simulator"` field on the reading — not just a UI comment.
- Gate entirely behind an explicit Dev Mode toggle — never active by default, never silently substituted if real BLE fails.
- **Design check:** confirm swapping in real BLE later requires changing only the data-source component, zero backend/schema changes. If any backend change would be required, fix the decoupling before continuing.

**Exit criterion:** simulator readings flow through `/api/health` identically to a real BLE reading would, visibly labeled DEV/SIMULATED end-to-end.

